# Input
```ts
/* should generate diagnostics */
withSpaces.replaceAll(/\s+/ as RegExp, ",");

const typed: RegExp = /\s+/;
withSpaces.replaceAll(typed, ",");

const asserted = /\s+/i satisfies RegExp;
withSpaces.replaceAll(asserted!, ",");

withSpaces.replaceAll(new RegExp("\\s+", "i" as const), ",");
withSpaces.replaceAll(new RegExp("\\s+", ("i")), ",");

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.ts:2:23 lint/nursery/useGlobalRegexInReplaceAll ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × This regular expression passed to replaceAll() is missing the g flag.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ withSpaces.replaceAll(/\s+/ as RegExp, ",");
      │                       ^^^^^
    3 │ 
    4 │ const typed: RegExp = /\s+/;
  
  i When replaceAll() receives a regular expression without the g (global) flag, it throws a TypeError instead of replacing text.
  
  i Add the g flag to the regular expression, or use replace() to replace only the first match.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

